amux cloud — reach this machine through Harness cloud

usage: amux cloud <command>

The cloud connection (provider mode) dials out to Harness over TLS, registers
this machine and serves agent panes over that one connection, so the Harness
web dashboard and phone app reach it from anywhere. A registration owned by
your account is your personal compute pool of kind "machine"; amux cloud
status and amux doctor print its provider id. See docs/remote-provider.md.

commands:
  connect [flags]       connect this machine to Harness cloud: config file plus a user service (survives reboot)
  status                the cloud connection: config, token, service, last registration and heartbeat
  disconnect            stop and remove the user service (the config file is kept)
  run [<orchestrator-addr>] [flags]
                        run the cloud connection in the foreground (provider mode)
  revoke --yes [flags]  permanently revoke this provider's broker registration and relay access
  enroll <command>      let Harness cloud connect devices, up to a ceiling (off by default)
  wake <command>        content-free cloud wake-ups for connected devices (opt-in)

examples:
  amux cloud connect --orchestrator orch.example.com:7443 --token-file ~/.config/amux/provider.token
  amux cloud status

Run 'amux cloud <command> --help' for details.
